      "explanation": [
        {
          "text": "The 2012 Statistical Abstract (Table 366) lists the highest points for each state, showing that only a handful of states (e.g., Florida at 345 ft, Delaware at 448 ft) are below 1,000 ft while the vast majority, such as Mount Mitchell at 6,684 ft and many others, exceed 1,000 ft. The Visual Capitalist article explicitly notes that only five states are below 1,000 ft, confirming that most state high points exceed that elevation.",
